Card sent as spam via email.
I tried to draw it with a bit higher quality, but...
Since I drew it with no feeling, just a sense of "I have to draw it!",
it felt like a mannequin. {{IMG:2}}
 
No theme... {{IMG:3}} No feeling... {{IMG:4}} No fun..{{IMG:5}}
 
Ah.. it just turned into a drawing that made me think, "This isn't it..." {{IMG:6}}
 
Anyway, Merry Merry Merry Christmas. {{IMG:7}}
 
Thanks to this, I sent out 8 "happy mails"...
(Group emails are treated as one, I see)
I was able to put 800 won into my piggy bank.
(Is this the only effect I got... {{IMG:8}})
 
Anyway, 2007... With this, the feeling of Bye~ Bye~ is strong.

{{IMG:1}}

Today, when I visited the hospital, they gave me a large deer in a bag. {{IMG:2}}
Am I supposed to light it up in front of my door when I get home? {{IMG:3}}
I was already thinking I should buy a Christmas tree since Christmas is approaching, but Eunhye beat me to it.

It feels strange to suddenly write my wife's name on the blog... {{IMG:4}}

Today, during the presidential debate, when candidate Moon asked if I had ever called my wife by her name, it struck a chord with me. I realized it wasn't right to insist on using the term "my wife" (집사람) even on my blog. From now on, I've decided to write her name on the blog again, and this is the first time I'm doing it.

It was a name I desperately wanted to call when I was pursuing her (thinking back, I really did follow her around a lot), and a name that made my heart pound just by hearing or saying it, yet it feels unfamiliar after only a year. Habits are truly frightening, it seems.

Eunhye also said she liked being called by her name...
But when she calls me "Byeongseogi oppa," it still makes me smile.

Swept up in the 2007 presidential election, it seems I've even forgotten about Christmas.
At times like these, we shouldn't forget that many people feel lonely.
In our church, which serves many elderly members, holidays definitely seem to be approached with more caution. {{IMG:5}}

But isn't it a joyful day commemorating the arrival of Jesus?
And while we're at it, let's reflect on Jesus's will, look around us,
and most importantly, look back on the year, even experiencing some frustration. {{IMG:6}}
In commemoration of installing Rudolph in the house, I'm writing a Christmas preparation post.

I tried to put some winter-themed music on my blog, but I don't have any. {{IMG:7}}
The tens of thousands of won worth of music I bought when I was active on my mini-homepage turned out to be useless.

From a user's perspective, this is pure tyranny.
In the end, I bought the same music I already had on my mini-homepage again.

| {{IMG:8}} |
| --- |
| Winter Light-Sarah Bri.. |
| Winter Light-Sarah Bri.. |
| {{IMG:15}} |

From Naver's perspective, it's not really a structure that makes money from selling items, so music revenue is extremely minimal. Nevertheless, the idea of selling internet music, which started with Cyworld, was an excellent one, but the limitation that each music file cannot be used across different portals seems to be a problem. {{IMG:16}}

There's a rumor that music prices are going up again. Gasoline prices are rising, transportation costs are rising, medical insurance is rising, and is it only my allowance and income that can't keep pace? {{IMG:17}}

Anyway, most of the music revenue doesn't even go to the portals.
Well, the record labels are already in an uproar because albums aren't selling, so if portals were to make them compatible, they'd surely cause a fuss... {{IMG:18}}

I said I was writing a Christmas preparation post, but I ended up venting another complaint... {{IMG:19}}

I received an email asking me to write about my achievements for the year.
I wanted to write "pointless work," but if I did that, it would probably be hard to support the family I've worked so hard to build...

Rudolph. What did I really do? {{IMG:20}}
